<devicesets>
<deviceset name="WE-XHMI_4020" urn="urn:adsk.eagle:component:42916910/5" prefix="L" library_version="10">
<description>&lt;B&gt;WE-XHMI SMT Power Inductor&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/b&gt;Shielded&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Characteristicscs&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt; Flat wire coil for low copper losses
&lt;br&gt; Composite core material allows high saturation currents
&lt;br&gt; Compact design
&lt;br&gt; Magnetically shielded
&lt;br&gt; High current capability and handles high transient current spikes
&lt;br&gt; Low leakage flux noise
&lt;br&gt; Operating temperature: -40°C up to +125°C
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;WE-XHMI Performance:&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt; Operating temperature: -55°C up to +150°C
&lt;br&gt;Optimized for ultra low RDC and AC losses to enhance efficiency and minimize self-heating
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;WE-XHMI:&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt; Operating temperature: -40°C up to +125°C
&lt;br&gt;Reliable inductor featuring a balanced combination of low losses and high current capability
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Applications&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt; DC/DC-converter for high current power supplies
&lt;br&gt; DC/DC-converter for Field Programmable Gate Array (FPGA)
&lt;br&gt; Power supplies for mobile devices
&lt;br&gt; POL-converters
&lt;br&gt; Mainboards/ graphic cards
&lt;br&gt; Battery powered devices
&lt;br&gt; Wireless communication devices
&lt;br&gt; Filter

&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.we-online.com/components/media/o14900v209%20FAMILY-WE-XHMI.jpg" title="Enlarge picture"&gt;
&lt;img src="https://www.we-online.com/components/media/o14900v209%20FAMILY-WE-XHMI.jpg" width="320"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;
Details see: &lt;a href="www.we-online.com/catalog/WE-XHMI/?utm_source=eagle_model&amp;utm_medium=description_link&amp;utm_campaign=eisos_eagle"&gt;www.we-online.com/en/components/products/WE-XHMI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;


Updated by Ella Wu 2024-09-18&lt;br&gt;
2024 (C) Würth Elektronik</description>
